work spans the strategy's Notebooks, Data Science Pipelines, and\n104\t  Dashboard components (the format is consumed by all three), but is assigned\n105\t  the single most-relevant canonical component **Notebooks**: the tutorials are\n106\t  predominantly notebooks and the pinned-image aspect maps to the workbench\n107\t  imagestreams that the Notebooks architecture context describes as maintained\n108\t  by the platform.\n109\t- E002 → component **Dashboard** (team RHOAI Dashboard), E003 → **Notebooks**\n110\t  (team Workbenches), E004 → **Data Science Pipelines** (team RHOAI Pipelines),\n111\t  E005 → **Documentation** (team assumed RHOAI Docs) — all verbatim canonical\n112\t  names from `.context/rhai-components.txt`.\n113\t- The **Documentation** component has no architecture-context file. No\n114\t  onboarding chain was generated: Documentation is a docs-process component\n115\t  delivered through the Red Hat docs content process (`docs-authoring`\n116\t  implementation type), not a new code component needing a repo or build\n117\t  pipeline.\n118\t\n119\t## Health Warnings\n120\t\n121\t1. **Missing strategy sections (non-blocking):** the strategy has no Impacted\n122\t   Teams table, no Dependencies table, no Acceptance Criteria section (no\n123\t   Given/When/Then with \"measured by\" clauses), and no Non-Functional\n124\t   Requirements. Owner teams were inferred from architecture context and epic\n125\t   acceptance criteria were derived from the HLRs.\n126\t2. **E003 size over the ~2-week guideline:** authoring and validating five\n127\t   tested notebook tutorials is estimated at roughly 2–3 sprints of content\n128\t   effort (the strategy provides no effort arithmetic). Kept whole because all\n129\t   five tutorials share one packaging format, one validation approach, and one\n130\t   content review pipeline — splitting them would duplicate format-conformance\n131\t   and validation setup and fragment a single content stream. Re-split trigger:\n132\t   if the tutorial set exceeds 3 sprints of effort, or any single tutorial\n133\t   grows its own engineering track (e.g., the RAG tutorial needs new sample\n134\t   infrastructure beyond a notebook), split E003 by journey group (workbench/\n135\t   data-prep vs training/deployment/RAG).\n136\t3. **Ongoing-maintenance scope trap (non-blocking):** HLR-2 requires tutorials\n137\t   \"tested against the current release\" — a one-time gate at delivery. The\n138\t   strategy is silent on re-validating tutorials against future releases;\n139\t   that operational treadmill is out of scope here and should be planned\n140\t   separately if wanted.\n141\t4. **Docs priority inversion flag (expected):** HLR-4 is P2 but E005 is P1 by\n142\t   the docs-authoring priority exception (strategy `priority: Major`). This is\n143\t   per-spec, not an inconsistency.\n144\t\n145\t## Tiered Delivery\n146\t\n147\tNot applicable — the strategy has no external dependencies with uncertain\n148\ttiming; all work is internal to the platform's teams.\n149\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9ea04903d04393a1","agent_id":"a83cefb5121400077","session_id":"6748621f-9ce4-492b-a6d6-554d05aa57d4","uuid":"ef44f41d-1eb2-498a-8712-acdb08809961","timestamp":"2026-10-26T17:27:01.720Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-83831f86ed2ec399","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9019 decomposition"}
