sh the specification where both content authors and the Dashboard\n52\t  gallery implementers can build against it.\n53\t\n54\t## Acceptance Criteria\n55\t\n56\t- The packaging format specification defines the tutorial metadata schema,\n57\t  the pinned image reference mechanism, and the contents of the validation\n58\t  manifest.\n59\t- A reference tutorial packaged per the format passes the format's own\n60\t  validation.\n61\t- Versioning independence is demonstrated: a conforming tutorial can be\n62\t  versioned and validated as a packaged artifact, with no Dashboard release\n63\t  required to add, update, or validate it.\n64\t\n65\t## HLR Traceability\n66\t\n67\t- HLR-3 (P1): A tutorial packaging format (metadata, pinned images,\n68\t  validation manifest) is defined so tutorials are versioned and testable\n69\t  independently of Dashboard releases. (Epic priority is P0 by inheritance:\n70\t  this format gates all P0 work in the strategy.)\n71\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9ea04903d04393a1","agent_id":"a83cefb5121400077","session_id":"6748621f-9ce4-492b-a6d6-554d05aa57d4","uuid":"5eb4485a-ab98-44d3-859c-182f611592b5","timestamp":"2026-10-26T17:27:04.175Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a5bcd7dc34801f89","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9019 decomposition"}
