sed\n51\t  interaction, feature administration), leaving specific configuration\n52\t  mechanics to the implementing team.\n53\t\n54\t## Acceptance Criteria\n55\t\n56\t- Given a user with a project, when they open the tutorial gallery, then\n57\t  curated tutorials are listed with their packaged metadata.\n58\t- Given a notebook tutorial listed in the gallery, when the user launches it,\n59\t  then a workbench is opened in their project with the tutorial notebook\n60\t  loaded.\n61\t- Given a pipeline tutorial listed in the gallery, when the user launches it,\n62\t  then the pipeline is imported into their project.\n63\t- Launching a tutorial into the user's project requires a single user action.\n64\t- A tutorial packaged per the tutorial packaging format is launchable by the\n65\t  gallery without gallery-side changes specific to that tutorial (validated\n66\t  with a tutorial packaged per the format).\n67\t\n68\t## HLR Traceability\n69\t\n70\t- HLR-1 (P0): The Dashboard has a tutorial gallery from which a user can\n71\t  launch a tutorial into their project (opening a workbench with the\n72\t  notebook, or importing the pipeline).\n73\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9ea04903d04393a1","agent_id":"a83cefb5121400077","session_id":"6748621f-9ce4-492b-a6d6-554d05aa57d4","uuid":"47317054-414a-482a-ba79-55dc279dc1d0","timestamp":"2026-10-26T17:27:04.767Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9d01c6d7f6e4198d","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9019 decomposition"}
